"""The flow scoreboard: every declared cross-module flow is proven at L2 or carries its reason.

The WORLD is the CS06 arrows table in `docs/corpus-schematics.md` -- forty directional arrows derived
from the declared semantic flows -- read by cell, not by pattern over the whole line. Every flow found
there must have an entry below and every entry must name a flow found there (reconciled both ways,
so a flow added to the corpus cannot pass silently and a retired one cannot linger).

An entry is either `l2`: the one test that makes the flow done -- a case that crosses both modules'
real doors through the binary -- named as `<file>::<fn>` and resolved to a `#[test]` in that file;
or `reason`: why it is not L2 yet and the slice it `lands_with`, optionally naming a `partial` test
that covers part of it. A partial is never counted as L2 (HEE3_MASTER_PLAN_20260926.md §5).

An entry may also name a `host` record (HT3; `hee3-evidence/T28/HO01-T3-20260928/FLOW-CONTRACT.md` §4): a committed
record of the flow run on the host against an installed release. It counts as L2 only while it is verified against
the tree and the release it names: (a) its `source_sha` is an ancestor of the tree, (b) nothing under `src`,
`Cargo.toml` or `Cargo.lock` changed since, (c) `dirty=0`, (d) every asserted line is present, (e) the engine digest
recomputed from the release directory equals the record's, and (f) the release manifest's `source_commit` is the
record's `source_sha`. A stale record, an absent one, or a release this machine does not hold is legible and not
red; a record that contradicts itself or its release is refused. Never a stored status.

Prints `flows=N l2=L host=H reasoned=R unexplained=U` and refuses any unexplained flow, any unresolved test,
any refused host record and an empty world. `--control` proves each refusal fires on its own diagnostic.

Run: python3 tools/check-flow-scoreboard [--control]
"""

